# visit-attribution core

- **Std-first:** do not add `[dependencies]` without an explicit human ask.
- `unsafe_code = forbid`. Clippy `all`/`pedantic`/`nursery`/`cargo` deny
  (`clippy.toml` cognitive complexity 5). Rustdoc `all = deny`. Supply chain:
  `deny.toml` + `.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml`.
- MSRV **1.74**. CI is stable-only—do not use post-1.74 syntax
  (`#[expect]`, `reason =`, `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` are 1.81+).
- `Cargo.lock` is gitignored on purpose (library crate).
- Verify before finishing Rust work:
  - `cargo fmt --all -- --check`
  - `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
  - `RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc --no-deps`
  - `cargo test --all-targets --all-features`
  - `cargo +1.74 test` when touching MSRV-sensitive syntax
  - `cargo deny check` when `deny.toml` or dependencies change
- `VisitAttributor` requires a ranker. Training needs preference pairs (true
  place among ≥2 candidates).
- Prefer `codegraph_explore` with this project path before broad greps when
  available.
- **Precedence:** surgical edits over drive-by refactors; formatting via the
  style skill + rustfmt hook; SOLID skill only when changing stage boundaries.
- Ask before expanding public re-exports in `src/lib.rs`.
